{"nodes": [{"id": "brainstorm_doc", "label": "brainstorm.md (Linee guida ecosistema tornei)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brainstorm_results_source_of_truth", "label": "Current Results as Source of Truth (standings as read model)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a70.1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every standing is recomputable from results; no score is an updated field. Not event sourcing: current state plus history."}, {"id": "brainstorm_frozen_config", "label": "Versioned Config Frozen at Use (copy, not reference)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a70.2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tournament keeps a resolved copy of ruleset and policy; configuration is frozen, code is not, so a fixed tiebreak bug changes past standings if recalculated."}, {"id": "brainstorm_pure_engine", "label": "Pure TypeScript Tournament Engine", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a70.3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pairing and standings know neither Nuxt nor the DB; takes participants, results, config; testable with fixtures. Versioned package, verifiable from CLI like the FIDE pairing checker."}, {"id": "brainstorm_seeded_outcomes", "label": "Seeded Randomness, Outcomes Saved as Facts", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a70.4", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Seed generated by the server, chosen by no one; seed and engine version serve to verify, not re-run. Same input gives same output, so 'regenerate' is useless by construction."}, {"id": "brainstorm_game_as_composition", "label": "Adding a Game = Writing a Composition", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a70.5", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No DSL, no interpreter; a rule missing from the catalog is a new module, i.e. code."}, {"id": "brainstorm_row_not_contract", "label": "DB Row Is Not the API Contract (row -> mapper -> DTO)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a70.6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brainstorm_pgboss_jobs", "label": "pg-boss for All Jobs (enqueued in same transaction)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a70 Stack", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Persistent cron runs once across instances; fromDrizzle(tx, sql) ties jobs to the change; Nitro tasks are experimental and per-instance."}, {"id": "brainstorm_sse_live", "label": "SSE Live with LISTEN/NOTIFY Fan-out", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a70 Stack", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "30s keepalive under CapRover nginx 60s timeout, X-Accel-Buffering: no, ID-only payloads; a lost notification is fine since reconnecting clients reread the DB."}, {"id": "brainstorm_caprover_deploy", "label": "CapRover Deploy (always-on Node container)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a70 Stack", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Start with one instance, design for many; app container stateless, Postgres a separate CapRover app."}, {"id": "brainstorm_web_push", "label": "PWA Web Push (VAPID)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a70 Stack", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "On iPhone push only works with the app installed to Home Screen, so nothing that must arrive goes only via push."}, {"id": "brainstorm_smtp_mail", "label": "Email via SMTP (only from a job)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a70 Stack", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No irreplaceable provider: SMTP is a standard, provider in NUXT_MAIL_*; domain needs SPF, DKIM, DMARC."}, {"id": "brainstorm_better_auth_org", "label": "Better Auth organization Plugin", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a70 Stack, \u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brainstorm_player_identity", "label": "Player Identity Rules (on-the-fly, unclaimed, claim token)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No profile merge ever; the only defense is search-with-fuzzy-match before create. Claiming is not a merge."}, {"id": "brainstorm_anonymization", "label": "Removal = Anonymization", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Results are tournament facts and stay; Player becomes 'removed player' so closed standings don't change."}, {"id": "brainstorm_accepted_risks", "label": "Accepted Privacy Risks (minors, ownership)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a72 Rischi accettati", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Invite-only platform without privacy consultant; under-14 accounts and public minor profiles accepted, to revisit before public opening. Mitigations: noindex on minor profiles, warning on creation."}, {"id": "brainstorm_two_level_ruleset", "label": "Two-Level Ruleset (Module Catalog + Composition)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Catalog is engine code changed by deploy; composition is a choice of modules and params by platform or organizer. Valibot schema generated from catalog drives validation and the creation form."}, {"id": "brainstorm_catalog_categories", "label": "Catalog Categories (result shape, points, tiebreak, list, operational)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brainstorm_phase_architecture", "label": "Phase Architecture (ordered list in, ordered list out)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Input order is seeding, output order is standings; enables chaining. Each phase must linearize; final standings compose backward; operational settings are per phase."}, {"id": "brainstorm_no_rematch_scope", "label": "No-Rematch Scope = Chain of Phases Inheriting Opponent History", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brainstorm_bracket_seeding_modes", "label": "Groups-to-Bracket Seeding (overall_standing / fixed_cross)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brainstorm_rematch_warning", "label": "Round Limit Warning (rounds > players/2)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a75, \u00a710", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "System warns, never prevents; recalculated at every drop since drops lower the limit."}, {"id": "brainstorm_tournament_lifecycle", "label": "Tournament Lifecycle (draft -> published -> registration_open -> checkin_open -> running -> finished / cancelled)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a75 Ciclo di vita", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pause is a round-clock property, not a tournament state."}, {"id": "brainstorm_timezone_temporal", "label": "Per-Tournament IANA Timezone and Temporal Date Math", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a75 Date e fusi orari", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recurrences in local time, calendar offsets not durations, day deadlines end-of-day in tournament TZ, 'compatible' disambiguation for DST; native Temporal on Node 26, polyfill in frontend."}, {"id": "brainstorm_three_axes", "label": "Three Orthogonal Registration Axes (seat, attendance, play)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Compressing them makes 'how many still in play at round 3' unanswerable; participant count needs three views."}, {"id": "brainstorm_waitlist_offer", "label": "Waitlist Promotion by Expiring Offer", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Offer valid until 'tomorrow same time' in tournament TZ or check-in opening; seat reserved during the offer."}, {"id": "brainstorm_checkin_freeze", "label": "Check-in Opening as Single Freeze Point", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One moment ends cancellations and automatic offers; no-check-in at start is a no_show drop kept in history."}, {"id": "brainstorm_weighted_blossom", "label": "Weighted Blossom Maximum Matching Pairing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 Motore di abbinamento", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All rules become edge weights; always produces a complete pairing; avoids greedy dead-ends since there is no regenerate button."}, {"id": "brainstorm_lexicographic_priorities", "label": "Lexicographic Pairing Priorities (cardinality > no 2nd bye > no rematch > quadratic score diff > side > cosmetic)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each level outweighs the max sum of all lower levels; integer weights in BigInt or under 2^53. Second bye judged worse than a rematch."}, {"id": "brainstorm_manual_override", "label": "Manual Pairing Override with Mandatory Reason", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a77", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Warns but never prevents; organizer is the authority in the room. Kept despite EventLink removing manual pairings for fraud; reason in history deemed sufficient."}, {"id": "brainstorm_bye_origins", "label": "Two Bye Origins (structural, premium)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 Bye", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bye is always a full win; opponent dropping after pairing is not a bye."}, {"id": "brainstorm_round_lifecycle", "label": "Round Lifecycle (generate -> publish -> start; draft|published|started|closed|cancelled)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 Ciclo di vita del round", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cancelling marks pairings and results as cancelled and discards the snapshot; nothing is deleted. Cheap only because standings are a read model."}, {"id": "brainstorm_result_entry", "label": "Result Entry and Dispute Handling", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 Risultati", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One result row per match; first entry valid, contradictory second entry goes to history as rejected attempt and sets disputed. No-show is a loss followed by a drop."}, {"id": "brainstorm_repairing_diff", "label": "Re-pairing Proposal with Diff (same seed)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 Risultati", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brainstorm_tournament_history", "label": "Tournament History (app-written, same transaction, INSERT/SELECT only)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 Storico del torneo", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Trigger can't see app user or reason; single table per tournament; records also intentions that don't change state."}, {"id": "brainstorm_team_blind_lineup", "label": "Team Blind Simultaneous Lineup", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 Squadre", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brainstorm_clock_as_fact", "label": "Clock as DB Fact ({ endsAt, pausedMs, status } + server now)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 Tempo", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No server setInterval; client computes offset once and counts locally, no drift; SSE sends only state changes. Same logic as RoundTimer."}, {"id": "brainstorm_two_level_roles", "label": "Two-Level Roles (org owner/admin; tournament head_judge/judge/scorekeeper)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 Ruoli", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No tournament 'organizer' role; Better Auth lacks per-resource permissions so tournament roles are our own table. Playing judge is an off-by-default tournament option, a match-level permission check."}, {"id": "brainstorm_online_only", "label": "Online Only with Paper Fallback", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 Sala senza rete", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Offline writes would contradict server seed, single outcome per round, same-transaction history and first-result rule; offline and manual pairings were 90% of WER maintenance."}, {"id": "brainstorm_notifications", "label": "Notification Matrix (push + in app, email for seat offers)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 Notifiche", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brainstorm_data_model", "label": "Data Model Phase -> Round -> Match -> Board/Game", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a77 Modello dati", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Slot model kept even though v1 matches are always two entities, so FFA can arrive without rewriting matches, results and standings."}, {"id": "brainstorm_tiebreak_catalog", "label": "Tiebreak Catalog (OMW%, GW%, OGW%, VP, Buchholz, head-to-head, wins)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a78", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Floor and cap are function parameters (33% MTG, 25-75% Pokemon)."}, {"id": "brainstorm_bye_tiebreak_params", "label": "Bye in Tiebreaks as Two Independent Parameters", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a78 Il bye nei tiebreak", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each preset reproduces its game's official rules; free-tournament default exclude/excluded. Forfeit wins count as real opponents, deliberately diverging from FIDE."}, {"id": "brainstorm_exact_math", "label": "Standings Math Uses Only + - * /, min, max", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a78 Altre regole", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Math.pow and similar change across Node versions; values rounded to declared precision before comparison."}, {"id": "brainstorm_season_recalc", "label": "Season Recalculation Job with Credit Realignment", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a79, \u00a710", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Corrections apply in place even after season close and can change best-N of absent players; revocations and issuances in the same transaction; spent credits stay spent."}, {"id": "brainstorm_ranking_best_n", "label": "Best-N Season Ranking with Size Quotas", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a73 Ranking policy", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Uses placement, not path; size multiplier is the only correction. Ranking is a selection, not a sum."}, {"id": "brainstorm_glicko_rating", "label": "Glicko Rating (separate from circuit points)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a79, \u00a710", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only number not a pure function of results: RD decays with inactivity, needs periodic job or lazy calc."}, {"id": "brainstorm_capacity_three_states", "label": "Three-State Capacity (occupied / offer-reserved / free) DB Constraint", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a710", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bug source number one; registered < cap is wrong by construction; PGlite single connection won't surface races in dev."}, {"id": "brainstorm_scanner_safe_links", "label": "Scanner-Safe One-Time Links (GET confirm, POST consume)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a710", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Mail scanners like Microsoft Safe Links open links before the recipient; scanners don't submit forms."}, {"id": "brainstorm_v1_scope", "label": "v1 Scope: First Real Tournament 29 Nov 2026 (free, swiss + top cut, individual)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a711", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Invite-only first release; accounts created by hand, results entered by staff only, no print or offline."}, {"id": "brainstorm_milestones", "label": "Milestones M0 Walking Skeleton -> M1 Swiss -> M2 Top Cut -> M3 Dress Rehearsal", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a711 Milestone", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brainstorm_post_v1_roadmap", "label": "Post-v1 Ordered Roadmap", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a711 Dopo la v1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "readme_pglite_dev", "target": "brainstorm_caprover_deploy", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a70 Stack", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_pglite_dev", "target": "brainstorm_capacity_three_states", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a710", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "brainstorm_doc", "target": "glossario_doc", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "intro", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "brainstorm_doc", "target": "revisione_brainstorm_doc", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "intro", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "brainstorm_doc", "target": "claude_doc", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a70.6", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "brainstorm_results_source_of_truth", "target": "glossario_standings_snapshot", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/brainstorm.md", "source_location": "\u00a78 Snapshot", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "brainst